1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:07,850
A Little Fever Dream Book. The Very Big World Problem. A Helpful Guide to Classroom Geography.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:13,875
Chester Antialiased liked to look at things very closely.

3
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:22,525
He leaned in to see if the world was rendered in 16-bit, but his blocky chin made a very analog impact.

4
00:00:22,775 --> 00:00:27,625
A tiny crack appeared right in the middle of the Atlantic Ocean.

5
00:00:27,875 --> 00:00:34,200
It was a very budget-friendly globe, which meant the continents were mostly suggestions.

6
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:38,125
It also smelled faintly of old pennies.

7
00:00:39,625 --> 00:00:43,250
Marisol and Winston saw the crack too.

8
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:51,075
They decided to be seen cooperating, as it was the most socially acceptable way to spend a Tuesday.

9
00:00:51,455 --> 00:00:54,533
[MARISOL] We must replace it before the next bell rings!

10
00:00:54,913 --> 00:01:02,938
They decided to work together, as it is the most efficient way to ensure no one person takes all the blame.

11
00:01:03,188 --> 00:01:06,538
They were very happy to be seen together.

12
00:01:08,042 --> 00:01:15,242
Marisol decided that since she was the only one with a ruler, she should be in charge of the vision.

13
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:20,467
She spent an hour making a list of requirements for a new globe.

14
00:01:20,847 --> 00:01:26,978
[MARISOL] Winston, I have found a task suited to your particular temperament: alphabetizing these footnotes.

15
00:01:27,358 --> 00:01:34,533
The list included three separate categories for the specific shade of beige used in the Sahara.

16
00:01:36,042 --> 00:01:40,767
The local hobby shop was filled with many wonderful things.

17
00:01:41,017 --> 00:01:46,692
However, a small wind-chime by the door made a very loud tinkling sound.

18
00:01:47,072 --> 00:01:51,051
[WINSTON] Goodness, it is positively deafening in here!

19
00:01:51,431 --> 00:01:54,606
He found the noise quite intrusive.

20
00:01:54,856 --> 00:02:02,456
He wondered if the shop offered a silent-shopping experience, or perhaps a small, soundproof box to sit in.

21
00:02:03,958 --> 00:02:08,183
Marisol decided a store-bought globe was too common.

22
00:02:08,433 --> 00:02:14,558
She suggested they contact the professional cartography guild for a custom model.

23
00:02:14,938 --> 00:02:21,391
[MARISOL] The guild's office is in a quiet basement, which will prevent Winston from making those distressing little noises.

24
00:02:21,771 --> 00:02:29,046
Winston agreed, as he found Marisol's insistence on total control to be very comforting.

25
00:02:30,583 --> 00:02:37,533
Marisol spent ten minutes explaining the exact scale and longitude requirements to Chester.

26
00:02:37,783 --> 00:02:42,233
She used many big words and a very complex chart.

27
00:02:42,613 --> 00:02:45,616
[MARISOL] Do you understand the importance of the ratio, Chester?

28
00:02:45,996 --> 00:02:48,621
Chester nodded politely.

29
00:02:48,871 --> 00:02:55,471
He was currently wondering if he could fit a whole slice of pizza into his inventory slot.

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,700
Chester visited the guild to place the order.

31
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:07,975
He tried to repeat Marisol's complex ratio, but he forgot the word for globe halfway through.

32
00:03:08,355 --> 00:03:10,915
[CHESTER] I suppose 'The Big One' will do.

33
00:03:11,295 --> 00:03:15,570
The guild members admired his bold minimalism.

34
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:21,370
They had never been asked to build a map that required its own zoning permit.

35
00:03:22,875 --> 00:03:27,225
While the globe was being built, Winston found a new hobby.

36
00:03:27,475 --> 00:03:32,275
He mapped the quietest zones of the school for their collective safety.

37
00:03:32,655 --> 00:03:37,826
[WINSTON] The library is quite peaceful, provided one ignores the sound of people breathing.

38
00:03:38,206 --> 00:03:45,481
He found that the most peaceful place was wherever Chester happened to be standing, as Chester rarely spoke.

39
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:53,525
Marisol decided the geography section of the classroom needed a complete makeover.

40
00:03:53,775 --> 00:04:00,500
She spent her evening color-coding textbooks to match the prestige of their upcoming globe.

41
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:03,411
[MARISOL] Everything must be in its proper place.

42
00:04:03,791 --> 00:04:10,216
It is amazing how much one can achieve when one views sleep as a personal failure.

43
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:15,075
The delivery day finally arrived.

44
00:04:15,325 --> 00:04:20,925
A very large truck pulled up to the school, followed by a heavy-duty crane.

45
00:04:21,175 --> 00:04:25,325
The globe was so large it had its own weather system.

46
00:04:25,575 --> 00:04:33,675
It was a very impressive piece of geography, though the South Pacific was currently experiencing a mild drizzle.

47
00:04:34,055 --> 00:04:37,703
[WINSTON] My, it is a bit larger than I imagined.

48
00:04:39,208 --> 00:04:43,658
The trio tried to sneak the globe through a side window.

49
00:04:44,038 --> 00:04:48,956
[MARISOL] Winston, your unique proportions make you the perfect tool for this task!

50
00:04:49,336 --> 00:04:54,836
She admired how Winston's small frame made him an excellent human wedge.

51
00:04:55,086 --> 00:05:01,311
She gave him a very firm push, as she enjoyed seeing how much pressure the glass could take.

52
00:05:02,833 --> 00:05:07,508
The crane driver started his engine to help push the globe.

53
00:05:07,758 --> 00:05:12,508
The roar of the motor sounded like a thunderstorm to Winston.

54
00:05:12,758 --> 00:05:17,933
In his fright, he accidentally triggered the school-wide lockdown alarm.

55
00:05:18,313 --> 00:05:19,471
[WINSTON] Mercy!

56
00:05:19,851 --> 00:05:25,876
He found the alarm to be a very loud way of reminding him that he was still alive.

57
00:05:27,417 --> 00:05:31,267
The alarm rang loudly through the whole school.

58
00:05:31,517 --> 00:05:38,717
All the students and teachers stood in a circle, staring up at the giant globe stuck in the window.

59
00:05:39,097 --> 00:05:41,097
[TEACHER] What a curious decoration.

60
00:05:41,477 --> 00:05:47,027
It was a very public mistake, which is the most expensive kind of mistake.

61
00:05:47,407 --> 00:05:49,967
[TEACHER] The globe's placement really opened up the room.

62
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:55,750
The Principal walked up to the globe and beamed with pride.

63
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:01,275
He thought the students had organized a surprise donation for the school.

64
00:06:01,655 --> 00:06:05,095
[PRINCIPAL] This shall be the centerpiece of our new Global Initiative!

65
00:06:05,475 --> 00:06:14,525
Chester nodded politely, though he was currently trying to remember if the world was actually round or just a very large pancake.

66
00:06:16,042 --> 00:06:20,667
Marisol did not want anyone to know she had not planned this.

67
00:06:20,917 --> 00:06:27,167
She quickly volunteered to lead a neighborhood association committee for urban planning.

68
00:06:27,547 --> 00:06:31,607
[MARISOL] I shall redraw the street layout, as it lacks a certain direction.

69
00:06:31,987 --> 00:06:39,837
Several residents now believed their driveways were actually public parks, but the maps looked very tidy.

70
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:45,950
Winston suggested the globe be moved to the town square.

71
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:54,425
He felt this was the maximum distance he could possibly be from Marisol while still being seen to participate.

72
00:06:54,805 --> 00:06:57,402
[WINSTON] It will be a sanctuary of peace.

73
00:06:57,782 --> 00:07:03,157
Marisol agreed, as long as she could choose the color of the pedestal.

74
00:07:04,667 --> 00:07:08,592
The town held a grand parade to move the globe.

75
00:07:08,842 --> 00:07:18,142
They were a most compatible group, in the way that three different types of mismatched luggage are all compatible with the same overhead bin.

76
00:07:18,392 --> 00:07:25,217
They walked in a very orderly line, with exactly three feet of safety between each person.

77
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:31,325
At the unveiling, Chester noticed a small smudge on the map.

78
00:07:31,575 --> 00:07:39,425
He leaned in too close to inspect it and accidentally pushed a precarious support beam with his blocky chin.

79
00:07:39,675 --> 00:07:45,525
Chester tried to resize the smudge, but he found himself completely off-axis.

80
00:07:45,775 --> 00:07:51,825
The structure groaned and rolled away, flattening the mayor's podium and a cheese stall.

81
00:07:53,333 --> 00:08:00,833
The giant globe rolled down the main street and crashed through the school gates, smashing into the classroom wall.

82
00:08:01,083 --> 00:08:07,033
This created a brand new window that revealed the original broken globe.

83
00:08:07,283 --> 00:08:12,883
It had only one tiny crack, which was now the most accurate part of the map.

84
00:08:13,263 --> 00:08:15,705
[WINSTON] Look! It is still here.

85
00:08:17,208 --> 00:08:22,233
The teacher smiled and asked them to put a piece of tape over the crack.

86
00:08:22,483 --> 00:08:33,033
The three friends walked away together, each cherishing the wonderful silence that comes when one has finally run out of things to say to another person.

87
00:08:33,283 --> 00:08:39,808
They were perfectly aligned, much like two tectonic plates just before a catastrophic shift.
